Alongside my studies I manage e-commerce and technology at Divine Tree, which keeps me close to how software behaves once it meets catalogues, marketplaces, fulfilment and customers.', 'I started with the web — HTML, CSS and JavaScript — and kept following the problems. That led to React and Node on the web, Flutter on mobile, and Python for computer vision and machine learning. Hackathons, college projects and client-style work taught me to ship under constraints; running real e-commerce operations taught me what software has to survive after launch.', 'Web applications, mobile apps, AI integrations and internal tools. Some are products I am building for the long run, some are client-oriented software, and some are experiments I use to learn a technology properly.', 'Start from the problem, not the stack. Ship something small that works, put it in front of real users, and let what they do decide what gets built next. Understand the business well enough that the software fits how people already work.', array['Product engineering', 'Full-stack development', 'AI agents and automation', 'SaaS', 'E-commerce technology', 'Mobile applications', 'Computer vision', 'Business operations']::text[], 'Ahmedabad, India', null, '', null, 'Independent technology studio', 'Turning ideas into intelligent digital experiences.', 'I''m Jeet Patel — a developer and product builder exploring software engineering, AI, automation, and digital products. I build solutions that connect technology with real-world problems.', array['Building technology that turns ideas into reality.', 'Ideas. Engineering. Impact.', 'From concepts to products.']::text[])
